  "strDescriptionEN": "Ali Bina Demb\u00e9l\u00e9 (born 5 January 2004) is a French professional footballer who plays as a right-back for Serie A club Torino.\r\n\r\nCareer\r\nA youth product of FC du Bourget, Demb\u00e9l\u00e9 signed a youth contract with Troyes on 15 June 2017, and was promoted to their reserves in 2021. In October 2022, he transferred to Torino where he played in their Primavera side. In the summer of 2023, he was promoted to the Torino senior side and was part of their preseason. On 1 September 2023, he moved to Venezia on a season-long loan. He made his senior and professional debut with Venezia in a 4\u20133 Serie B win over Parma on 7 October 2023.\r\n\r\nUpon his return from loan, he made his Serie A debut for Torino on 17 August 2024 in an away game against AC Milan. He substituted Raoul Bellanova in the 88th minute with Torino ahead 2\u20130, AC Milan scored twice in the remaining time to equalize.\r\n\r\nPersonal life\r\nBorn in France, Demb\u00e9l\u00e9 is of Malian descent.",
